      "title": "Timetable Officer Job",
      "description": "Timetable Officer Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Video Is Your AI Resume Making You Invisible to Recruiters? | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Timetable Officer Timetable Officer at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary 3+ years managing and coordinating timetabling/scheduling/rostering in a complex environment. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent). Proficiency in scheduling software (e.g., Timetabler). Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Contract • Full-time • Mid-level Description Fixed term contract until 17 December 2027, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to coordinate critical timetabling and scheduling functions that support teaching and learning across the University College. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role The Timetable Officer is responsible for developing, coordinating, and maintaining class timetables, room scheduling, and related systems to support the effective delivery of teaching, learning, and campus operations across Excelsia. Primary responsibilities include: To develop, maintain, and optimise class timetables and room scheduling to ensure efficient operations and timetabling service delivery. To collaborate with internal departments, stakeholders, and system users to produce accurate and accessible timetables that meet organisational and regulatory requirements. To manage and support Excelsia’s timetabling software system/s and provide assistance and training to staff and students in their effective use. To prepare and publish timetables in liaison with the various internal stakeholders. To administer room bookings for staff and students. Administer Car park booking system for students. To maintain quality requirements including writing and updating procedures and forms relevant to the role and timetabling requirements of Excelsia. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Possession of a relevant degree level qualification, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience/ training Demonstrated experience (3+ years) managing and coordinating timetabling, scheduling, and/or rostering in a complex environment. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent) would be an advantage. Proven experience in scheduling, planning, or administrative roles. Strong attention to detail and organisational skills. Proficiency in scheduling software (e.g., Timetabler). Excellent communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder liaison skills. Ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Analytical mindset with problem-solving capabilities. An understanding of current and emerging trends in higher education. Technological literacy in a wide range of desktop applications to support reporting and analysis role requirements. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education, and much more. This full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the