      "title": "Chief Research Officer Job",
      "description": "Chief Research Officer Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Video Is Your AI Resume Making You Invisible to Recruiters? | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Chief Research Officer Chief Research Officer at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Demonstrated leadership capability including mentoring and coaching researchers to deliver. Proven ability to facilitate and manage organisational change. In-depth understanding of research governance, integrity, and compliance frameworks. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Senior Level Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to lead and grow Excelsia’s research strategy, impact and innovation. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role The Chief Research Officer provides strategic leadership of Excelsia University College’s research portfolio, driving research excellence, innovation, impact and growth in alignment with the University College’s mission and vision. Primary responsibilities include: To articulate, lead, and deliver Excelsia University College’s (Excelsia) research strategy, aligned with the mission and vision of Excelsia. To ensure the integrity and promote the quality of Excelsia’s research outputs and endeavours. To drive research impact, including but not limited to: securing external grant income, securing strategic research-aligned industry partnerships and alliances, leveraging appropriate use of artificial intelligence opportunities, fostering inter and multidisciplinary research initiatives, and building a research brand to influence and consolidate key themes to advance Excelsia’s reputation as a leading research institution. To provide strategic leadership and oversight of Excelsia’s research portfolio, and to lead and manage the Head of Research (Graduate Programs) and research staff, ensuring effectiveness, efficiency, and optimal research outcomes. To support academic career development and work to create a culture of excellence and sustainable growth in research and enterprise. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Earned Doctorate from an accredited and respected national or international University, preferably in a discipline area consistent with the College’s academic disciplinary expertise. Strong research record as evidenced by the securing of external funding and an excellent publication record, preferably in refereed journals. Five or more years of demonstrated excellent higher education management skills with an ability to administer research strategy at a higher education provider. Experience in leading a university department as well as involvement in institution academic governance will be an advantage. Demonstrated capability to develop, launch, review, and enhance programs with strong outcomes. Demonstrated leadership capability including mentoring and coaching researchers to deliver. Proven ability to facilitate and manage organisational change. In depth understanding of research governance, integrity, and compliance frameworks. Demonstrated experience as strategic thinker with proven ability to both prioritise critical goals and execute strategies in the successful achievement of goals within budget and time frame constraints. Ability to demonstrate high integrity, vision, innovation, energy and enthusiasm for the mission, vision and values of the College and to be self-motivated in a fast pace changing environment. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education, and much more. This full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact 