    "https://employmenthero.com/jobs/position/excelsia-university-college-chief-academic-officer-agjgn/": {
      "title": "Chief Academic Officer Job",
      "description": "Chief Academic Officer Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Video Is Your AI Resume Making You Invisible to Recruiters? | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Chief Academic Officer Chief Academic Officer at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Earned Doctorate from an accredited and respected national or international university, preferably aligned to Excelsia’s 5+ years of demonstrated excellent higher education management skills across multiple departments and multi-campus/ToL/\" Ability to develop, launch, review and enhance degree programs with strong student numbers and graduate outcomes Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Senior Level Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to lead academic excellence, innovation and strategic growth across the University College. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role The Chief Academic Officer provides strategic leadership of Excelsia’s academic portfolio, driving excellence in teaching, learning, research and student outcomes. Primary responsibilities include: To provide strategic leadership for teaching and learning, scholarship, research, course portfolio development and associated community engagement, aligned with the mission and vision of Excelsia University College (Excelsia), and achieving optimal outcomes for students. To provide leadership and oversight of the Heads of School, ELICOS Program Director, Deputy Chief Academic Officer, ensuring the effective, efficient and optimal management of the academic portfolio and supporting high-quality student learning, development and outcomes. To lead the implementation of relevant priorities and initiatives within the Strategic Plan. To be responsible for course development and review, and course portfolio development in collaboration with members of Management Committee. To articulate and communicate Excelsia’s academic vision to internal and external stakeholders, while ensuring the integrity, quality and continuous improvement of Excelsia’s academic programs. Oversees academic programs (development, delivery, review and improvement), faculty affairs and many academic support functions of Excelsia, embedded by a Christian worldview. Works to ensure the fulfilment of institutional mission and goals and provides academic vision and leadership. Contribute to leadership of Excelsia through active membership of the Management Committee and the Academic Board. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Earned Doctorate from an accredited and respected national or international University, preferably in a discipline area consistent with the Excelsia’s academic disciplinary expertise. Five or more years of demonstrated excellent higher education management skills with an ability to administer multiple departments at a higher education provider and working in a multi-disciplinary, multi-campus and online/accelerated education environment. Experience in leading a university department, with involvement new course and faculty development, as well as involvement in institution academic governance will be an advantage. Demonstrated capability to develop, launch, review and enhance degree programs with strong student numbers and graduate outcomes. Strong research record as evidenced by the securing of external funding and an excellent publication record, preferably in refereed journals. Demonstrated leadership capability including mentoring and coaching Department Heads to deliver. Proven ability to facilitate and manage organisational change. Demonstrable experience as strategic thinker with proven ability to both prioritise critical goals and execute strategies in the successful achievement of goals within budget and time frame constraints. Demonstrable success as a team player, collaborator and consensus builder who is proactive in conflict resolution. Ability to demonstrate high integrity, vision, innovation, energy and enthusiasm for the mission, vision and values of Excelsia and to be self-motivated in a fast pace changing environment. Strong oral and written communications skills and experience in preparing timely, clear and concise documentation. Proven time management skills and ability to work under pressure with minimal supervision. A commitment to lifelong learning. Knowledge of and ability to apply equal opportunity principles and work health and safety principles in the workplace. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education, and much more. This full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the Employment Hero Group by email, text, and social media channels about its services and activities. You may withdraw your consent at any time. See the Privacy Policy for information on how your data is processed. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the l