      "title": "Professional Experiences Coordinator",
      "description": "Professional Experiences Coordinator Job at Excelsia University College You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Video Is Your AI Resume Making You Invisible to Recruiters? | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending News Article How 500 Lunches With Strangers Led To A Winning Business Mindset 6 min read Video How to Explain a Resume Gap in an Interview (Without Apologising) | The Jobseeker Series Video Recruiters Judge Your Profile in 8 Seconds: Here’s How to Win | The Jobseeker Series Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Professional Experiences Coordinator Professional Experiences Coordinator at Excelsia University College Student Placements • Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Tertiary qualification/s in Education or equivalent. Experience sourcing education placements through networking and industry visits. Hold full Australian working rights. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Experienced Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to support the learning activities of students’ professional experience units Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community Due to continued growth at Excelsia University College, we are expanding our student placements team and are seeking additional team members to join us during this exciting period of growth. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: Providing administrative support to the Education Professional Experience Manager and students. Sourcing education placements through networking and industry visits. Maintaining industry partnerships to sustain education placements. Ensuring the learning activities of professional experience units are operated effectively and efficiently. Participation in student allocations process, meeting with students, liaising with placement sites. Facilitating preparation of document completion in the LMS for moderation and final grades. Providing feedback and suggesting potential improvements to the Education Professional Experience program. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Tertiary qualification/s in Education or equivalent. Experience in an early childhood or initial teacher education environment. Experience in a higher education setting. Essential: Committed Christian, involved in a local congregation. Administration and project management skills. Proven organisational skills with the ability to multi-task, prioritise and meet deadlines. Must be able to work independently. Must uphold ethical integrity while performing duties of a sensitive nature including calculating student grades, handling petty cash, and maintaining confidentiality of personal details. Familiarity with Word, Excel, Power Point, and Outlook. Experience with a learning management system, particularly Moodle is strongly preferred. Demonstrated excellent interpersonal skills, ability to work appropriately with students, faculty, and administrators, independently as well as in a busy team environment. Hold full Australian working rights About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy flexible and family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a culturally rich environment, with opportunities to engage in spiritual devotions. Upskill with our substantial College tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families. Our employees have access to Thrive, a financial wellbeing app that offers instant access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education and much more. This full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the lands where we live, learn and work. © 2026 Employment Hero Pty Ltd. All rights reserved. Trust & Legal Centre Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Data Processing Addendum Cookie Policy Financial Disclosure Documents Close Clear Results for “ ” results Top Results Businesses Partners Employees Job Seekers Resources COMPANY About u