ndex Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Lecturer in Education (Early Childhood) Lecturer in Education (Early Childhood) at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary Hold a PhD in Early Childhood Education or be currently undertaking a PhD in Early Childhood Education. Demonstrated experience teaching at a tertiary level, including learning, scholarship and research. Demonstrated ability to teach online and face to face. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Qualified Description Full-time position Pennant Hills campus Lecturer Level B / Senior Lecturer Level C Be a part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community About the Role Primary responsibilities include: Teaching and unit coordination in agreed subject areas including managing and assessment of the units. Providing a quality education, care and support to the students. Ensuring the activities of the School are operated effectively and efficiently, Producing research and scholarship that informs learning and teaching, and curriculum innovation and development. Providing administrative support to the Head of School, Course Coordinators, and other academic staff. Building the profile and reputation of Excelsia with stakeholders, the community and potential students. Essential Criteria: Committed Christian, involved in a local congregation. Hold a PhD in Early Childhood Education or be currently undertaking a PhD in Early Childhood Education. Teaching experience and ECT qualification would be an advantage. Demonstrated experience in teaching at a tertiary level, learning, scholarship and research. Teaching experience in Early Childhood sector would be an advantage. Demonstrated expertise in ECEC and understanding of current and emerging trends in Australian Education. Excellent communication skills. Demonstrated ability to teach online and face to face. Awareness of and sensitivity to cultural diversity and ability to work with students, staff, and administrators cooperatively. Full Australian Working Rights. WWCC About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian Arts College. We are now a  part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your income with Salary Packaging scheme. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Enjoy our modern campus in Pennant Hills. Walk 5 minutes from transport or park onsite for free. Work in Great Place to Work ® Certified organisation How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community at Excelsia University College. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Early applications are encouraged. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your re