layer and share best practice across student experience, system upkeep, organisation, and planning Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Hold a post-secondary qualification Working experience, 2+ years in an administration role Working experience in a customer service role Essential: Committed Christian, involved in a local congregation Experience in business administration and/customer service Proven organisational skills with the ability to multi-task, prioritise, and meet deadlines Must have acute attention to detail and high level of accuracy Excellent oral and written communication skills Must be able to work independently Must uphold ethical integrity while performing duties of a sensitive nature including calculating student grades, and maintaining confidentiality of personal details Familiarity with Word, Excel, Power Point and Outlook Experience with a learning management system, particularly Moodle is strongly preferred Demonstrated excellent interpersonal skills, ability to work appropriately with students, faculty, and administrators, independently as well as in a busy team environment A commitment to lifelong learning Knowledge of and ability to apply equal opportunity principles and work health and safety principles in the workplace Full Australian Working Rights About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme Enjoy flexible and family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions Experience working in a culturally rich environment, with opportunities to engage in spiritual devotions Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education and much more. Learn more about why Excelsia is Great Place to Work ® Certified and why our staff love working at Excelsia here: https://greatplacetowork.com.au/companies/excelsia-college/ How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Tradition