      "title": "Senior Lecturer & Course Coordinator, Community Services and Youth Work",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer & Course Coordinator, Community Services and Youth Work Job at Excelsia University College You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Blogs Workplace stress risk assessment: are you actually okay going into the new year? 5 min read Blogs Career planning in your 20s, 30s, and 40s — what actually matters at each stage 5 min read Blogs The quiet signs you’re burning out at work (and what to do before it gets worse) 4 min read Blogs End-of-year exhaustion is real. Here’s how to actually rest over the holidays. 4 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending Blogs Workplace stress risk assessment: are you actually okay going into the new year? 5 min read Blogs Career planning in your 20s, 30s, and 40s — what actually matters at each stage 5 min read Blogs The quiet signs you’re burning out at work (and what to do before it gets worse) 4 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Senior Lecturer & Course Coordinator, Community Services and Youth Work Senior Lecturer & Course Coordinator, Community Services and Youth Work at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Full-time AI Job Summary PhD in a relevant field, or a master’s degree with active progress toward a PhD. At least 3 years’ experience in community work, such as social welfare, human services, social work or youth work. Ability to design, develop and implement academic programs that support strong student outcomes and engagement. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Permanent • Full-time • Senior Level Description Permanent, full-time position with free onsite parking A fantastic opportunity to lead the Master of Community Services and Youth Work program and contribute to excellence in teaching, research, and professional development. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: To ensure excellence in the development of students’ knowledge, skills and capabilities and in their preparation for life in community services or youth work post completion of their studies. To provide academic and strategic oversight, as well as direction and leadership to the Master of Community Services and Youth Work Program, and other nested degrees, in order to achieve excellence in: teaching and learning; research and scholarship; and professional and academic development amongst students and staff. To build the profile and reputation of the University College with stakeholders, the community and potential students and to play a leading role in promoting and representing the program within and external to the University College, and for developing and maintaining strategic relationships with external stakeholders and communities. With regard to the objectives above, activities must be aligned with: the vision, mission and values, and short term and long-term plans and objectives of the University College; policy guidelines as defined by relevant boards and committees; quality and compliance responsibilities commensurate with the University College registration and degree accreditation requirements. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Committed Christian involved in a local congregation. Hold a PhD (or holds a Masters and/or is working towards a PhD qualification) in community work, social welfare, human services, social work or a comparable field. Comprehensive experience (3+ years) in the community work field such as social welfare, human services, social work, or community services including mental health, disability, youth work and other relevant streams. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent) would be an advantage. Demonstrated ability to design, develop, and implement academic programs linked to good outcomes and high engagement. An understanding of current and emerging trends in community studies discipline, higher education, and student wellbeing. Technological literacy in a wide range of desktop applications to support reporting and analysis role requirements. Excellent oral and written communication skills, and confidence in presentations. Proven organisational skills with the ability to prioritise and meet deadlines. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Excelsia Benefits Maximise your “take home” income through our Salary Packaging scheme. Enjoy family friendly policies, providing generous leave and working conditions. Experience working in a spiritually rich environment, with opportunities to engage in devotions. Upskill with our substantial tuition discount to eligible staff and their immediate families to study Excelsia courses. Our employees have access to earned wages, the ability to save before you’re paid, financial education, and much more. This full-time position is based in Pennant Hills. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as a suitable applicant is found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release note