      "title": "Casual Education Lecturers Job",
      "description": "Casual Education Lecturers Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Blogs Career planning in your 20s, 30s, and 40s — what actually matters at each stage 5 min read Blogs The quiet signs you’re burning out at work (and what to do before it gets worse) 4 min read Blogs End-of-year exhaustion is real. Here’s how to actually rest over the holidays. 4 min read Guides and Playbooks AI skills assessment template for your team 2 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending Blogs Career planning in your 20s, 30s, and 40s — what actually matters at each stage 5 min read Blogs The quiet signs you’re burning out at work (and what to do before it gets worse) 4 min read Blogs End-of-year exhaustion is real. Here’s how to actually rest over the holidays. 4 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Jobs Education & Training Casual Education Lecturers Casual Education Lecturers at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Casual Apply now AI Job Summary Hold a PhD, Masters or postgraduate qualification in a relevant Education discipline. Maintain current teacher registration (NSW or equivalent). Have experience in tertiary-level teaching, supervision, or leadership in education. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Temporary • Casual • Qualified Pay Rate $90.49 AUD – $154.09 AUD (Hour) Description Casual lecturing opportunities commencing November 2026 Close to public transport with free onsite parking. Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About Us Excelsia University College is a Christian University College with academic and administrative staff from many Christian denominations. Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: Tutoring in agreed subject areas and managing teaching and assessment of units being delivered. Providing administrative support to the Head of School, Course Coordinator, and other academic staff. Participating in the administration, assessment, marking and examination of students. Areas of Education we are looking for Lecturers/Tutors: Early Childhood Education Primary and Secondary Education Masters of Education Masters of Education Leadership Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Hold a PhD, Masters or postgraduate qualification in a relevant Education discipline. Lecturing and teaching experience (3+ years experience would be an advantage). Current teacher registration (NSW or equivalent). Essential: Respect the Christian mission of Excelsia University College. Ongoing or recent teaching experience in Early Childhood, Primary, or Secondary Education and an understanding of current and emerging trends in Early Childhood Education. Experience in tertiary-level teaching, supervision, or leadership in education. Experience in online or blended teaching environments Ability to communicate effectively with students; ability to communicate and work effectively and cooperatively with colleagues. Technological literacy and experience in developing online communication tools and previous experience in online education is desirable. Demonstrated awareness of and sensitivity to diversity and ability to work with students, staff, and administrators, including pastoral skills in mentoring staff and supporting students. Flexibility to teach on Saturdays (highly desirable) and/or weekdays and evenings. This casual position is based in Pennant Hills. Learn more about why Excelsia is Great Place to Work ® Certified and why our staff love working at Excelsia here: https://greatplacetowork.com.au/companies/excelsia-college/ How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter specifying the unit/s you are able to teach directly via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the Employment Hero Group by email, text, and social media channels about its services and activities. You may withdraw your consent at any time. See the Privacy Policy for information on how your data is processed. We acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the lands where we live, learn and work. © 2026 Employment Hero Pty Ltd. All rights reserved. Trust & Legal Centre Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Data Processing Addendum Cookie Policy Financial Disclosure Documents Close Clear Results for “ ” 0 results Top Results Businesses (0) Partners (0) Employees (0) Job Seekers (0) Resources (0) COMPANY About us Careers News & Me