      "title": "HDR Supervisors Job",
      "description": "HDR Supervisors Job at Excelsia University College Skip to content You have been redirected to your preferred market of Australia . Clear preference × You're viewing our Australia site. Select your region to visit the most relevant site for you. Select region New Zealand United Kingdom Singapore Malaysia Canada (Français) Canada (English) × Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Ask Hero AI Learn Login Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker AU Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Get started Jobseeker Employee Employer Work Jobs Find the role Land the role Learn Login Australia Back Learn Trending Blogs Psychological safety at work: what it is, why it matters, and how to tell if you have it 5 min read Blogs Workplace stress risk assessment: are you actually okay going into the new year? 5 min read Blogs Career planning in your 20s, 30s, and 40s — what actually matters at each stage 5 min read Blogs The quiet signs you’re burning out at work (and what to do before it gets worse) 4 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Get Started Trending Blogs Psychological safety at work: what it is, why it matters, and how to tell if you have it 5 min read Blogs Workplace stress risk assessment: are you actually okay going into the new year? 5 min read Blogs Career planning in your 20s, 30s, and 40s — what actually matters at each stage 5 min read Resource Types Webinars & Events Salary Calculator Blogs & Guides Interview Prep Support Centre Career Advice All Resources Topics AI Best Practice Workplace Effectiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Jobs Education & Training HDR Supervisors HDR Supervisors at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Casual Apply now AI Job Summary Hold a PhD relevant to the candidate’s proposed research, or equivalent scholarly achievement, or at least the admission Show acceptable research activity over the past five years via publications, grants and/or HDR completions. Full Australian Working Rights. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type Within Australia • Temporary • Casual • Qualified Description Casual positions available, with remote working ability A fantastic opportunity to support research students undertaking their thesis Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role HDR Supervisors are to support student’s progress through their HDR thesis writing component of their Master by Research degree or Doctoral degree providing skilled supervision to candidates enrolled in higher degrees by research and participating in a supervisory panel responsible for the monitoring and advancement of the candidate’s research. Excelsia University College offers three master’s research degrees and one doctoral research degree across the School of Business and School of Education. The research degrees are: Master of Business Research (MBR) Master of Education Research (MER) Master of Education Research (MER – STEM) Doctor of Philosophy (Organisational Leadership) (PhD) Primary responsibilities include: Undertake necessary staff induction and training for HDR Supervision. Provide regular and informative HDR supervision meetings for students. Advise and assist the candidates to commence an original and feasible research program. Monitor student progression and undertake reporting and recommend actions as appropriate. Support the candidate in timely completion of the thesis research including thesis submission and examination. Ensure transparency and achieve agreement about authorship of publications. Provide support to build the capacity of the students in the areas below: academic writing, literature review, research proposal, time management, research project management, data analysis, preparation for research workshops and conferences, publications, career planning and development, and use of relevant software and other research skills issues, as relevant. Selection Criteria Essential requirements: Respect the Christian mission of Excelsia University College. Hold a Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in a field relevant to the candidate’s proposed research, or have an equivalent record of scholarly achievement, or a qualification at least at the level of the award for which the candidate is admitted. Show evidence of an acceptable level of research activity over the past five years in the form of publications, research grants and/or HDR completions as specified in the Excelsia University College Policy on Research Active Status. Full Australian Working Rights. Skills and Capabilities: An understanding of best practice in higher degree research and candidate supervision. Technological literacy in a wide range of desktop applications to support reporting and analysis role requirements. Excellent oral and written communication skills, and confidence in presentations. Proven organisational skills with the ability to prioritise and meet deadlines. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume and covering letter addressing the position criteria via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting Other 0 / 100 Additional comments (optional) 0 / 500 Your email (optional, for follow-up) Please enter a valid email address. Something went wrong. Please try again. Cancel Report COMPANY About us Careers News & Media Partners Hero Foundation GET IN TOUCH Contact us Request a demo SUPPORT Help Centre System status Release notes PRODUCT Employment OS HR & Compliance Recruitment Agent Payroll & Rostering HeroForce Benefits & Perks Integrations Case Studies Pricing LEARN Blog Events Webinars Factsheets Case Studies Templates Whitepapers Reports Press Releases PICK YOUR REGION Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia CONNECT in f 𝕏 ig ▶ STAY IN THE LOOP The latest employment law updates, product news and HR tips — straight to your inbox. * → I agree to receive marketing communications from Employment Hero. I can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking ‘Subscribe’ , you consent to receiving marketing from the Employment Hero Group by email, text, and social media channels about its services and activities. You may withdraw your cons